                <pb facs="0535" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg455"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Francis to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                            1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I was
                    accorded a special audience to-day by King Alexander, upon which occasion His
                    Majesty presented me to Her Majesty, Queen Draga. They both declared in
                    strongest terms their horror at the murder of President McKinley and their
                    sympathy for the American people in the great loss they have sustained by the
                    death of a chief so wise and so good. Their majesties inquired particularly
                    about Mrs. McKinley, and expressed for her the tenderest solicitude. King
                    Alexander was evidently much gratified when I informed him that I had been
                    requested by my Government in a cable dispatch received last evening to convey
                    to His Majesty Mrs. McKinley’s sincerest appreciation of his message of
                    condolence.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles S.
                    Francis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
